SiliconForest changes: recording is explicitly unsupported. The runner reports
unavailable and readiness returns NO with an NSError. Under Finch's one-object
result-callback convention, failure callbacks receive an NSError, never nil.
Void-only operations raise SFRecapUnsupportedOperationException with that error
in NSUnderlyingErrorKey; they never invoke a success-only completion block.
Parameter instances store data only and never record or complete a test.

Preview's observed mandatory imports name RPTTestRunner and
RPTActivationTestParameters. Its selector inventory includes isRecapAvailable,
runTestWithParameters:, setTestName:, and
initWithTestName:window:completionHandler:. Selector presence alone does not
establish a receiver or a full private Apple ABI. The activation class is new
open parameter storage using the same name/window/completion fields as Finch's
resize parameters. No claim of complete Apple Recap compatibility is made.

No Apple implementation, framework binary, SDK declaration, extracted asset or
application bytes are included in this provider. The cross-built probe has to
run on a separately authorized compatible runtime before behavioral validation
can be claimed. Building or exporting this output does not install it.


